# Java

Multi-module Maven enforces boundaries at compile time.

- `payment-domain` depends on nothing.
- `payment-application` depends only on `payment-domain`.
- Adapters depend on application and domain, never on each other.
- Only `payment-bootstrap` performs composition.

Forbidden in the domain: `org.springframework`, `jakarta.persistence`, `jakarta.servlet`, `javax.persistence`, `org.hibernate`, `com.fasterxml.jackson`, `org.apache.kafka`, `software.amazon.awssdk`, `java.sql`, `javax.sql`, `java.net.http`, `io.micrometer`, `org.slf4j`.

Forbidden in the application: `org.springframework`, `jakarta.persistence`, `org.hibernate`, `com.fasterxml.jackson`, `org.apache.kafka`, `software.amazon.awssdk`, `java.sql`, `java.net.http`.

JUnit 5 + AssertJ for behaviour, ArchUnit for structure, JaCoCo for coverage.